<title>SINGAPORE: Dai Hung consortium tenders to sell June crude.</title>
<headline>Dai Hung consortium tenders to sell June crude.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The consortium operating the Dai Hung crude field in Vietnam has issued a tender to sell at least one 450,000-barrel June-loading cargo, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on May 8 and an award will be made on the same day.</p>
<p>The Dai Hung sahareholders are Malaysia's state-owned Petronas, with 20 percent, Japan's Sumitomo Corp with 10.625 percent, France's Total SA with 10.625 percent and state-owned PetroVietnam, with 15 percent.</p>
<p>Petronas is in the process of buying out the 43.75 percent stake of Australia's Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
</text>
